before:
The supplied HTML is separate from the CSS.

```html
<div class="cards"><article>Water</article><article>Weather</article></div>
```

```css
.cards { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 12px; }
@media (min-width: 600px) { .cards { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } }
```

after:
The supplied HTML has two cards inside `.cards`. This CSS gives them one column, then two columns when there is room.
```css
.cards {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  gap: 12px;
}
@media (min-width: 600px) {
  .cards {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
  }
}
```
Each `1fr` gets an equal share of the available width.
